From: genetixteam <genetixteam@gmail.com>
Subject: econet-eth: PPE offload for wired->Wi-Fi flows with CPU egress

Do what the vendor hw_nat "ExtIf" path does: a flow that enters on the
wired port and leaves on another netdev (br-lan towards Wi-Fi clients)
is bound with the CPU as PSE egress port. The PPE still does the NAT and
the L2 rewrite (incl. VLAN/PPPoE removal); frames come back with crsn
HIT_BIND_FORCE_CPU and are handed straight to the egress device,
skipping the stack. Off by default:

  echo 1 > /sys/module/econet_eth/parameters/wifi_offload

Also refuse flows whose ingress is not the wired port (the upload
direction of Wi-Fi flows): the PPE never sees those packets, and
accepting them left Wi-Fi flows half "hardware offloaded".

New debugfs econet_ppe/diag counters: repl_ok_cpu, repl_rej_ingress,
rx_cpu_xmit, rx_cpu_nomatch.

